<title>USA: CELOX gets patent on ViaStem.</title>
<headline>CELOX gets patent on ViaStem.</headline>
<dateline>MINNETONKA, Minn. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>CELOX Laboratories Inc said Wednesday it was granted a patent on ViaStem, which it developed to improve storage of stem cells from bone marrow or peripheral blood while a patent receives chemotherapy.</p>
<p>Patients undergoing chemotherapy or radiation treatment for immunologic disorders or malignant disease would subsequently be infused with the stem cells containing ViaStem to restore the blood and immune systems.</p>
<p>CELOX, a biotechnology company, expects clinical trials to begin in late 1997.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
